# BB→Jugglebot reload: Ball Butler aims at Jugglebot's ACTIVE catch point and throws;
# Jugglebot (CATCH mode, hand armed by the existing catch_coordinator) tilts to align
# with the incoming ball and catches it. Orchestrated by reload_coordinator_node, which
# drives ONLY the sequence — trajectory_node plans all platform motion (build_catch),
# catch_coordinator_node arms the hand. Preconditions are checked before any ball flies
# (see reload_sequencer.py); the operator sets CATCH mode (the action does not switch
# modes). See plans/active/mvp-trajectory-bringup.md § Reload sequence.

float64 throw_delay_s          # delay from now to release; 0 => default 3.0 s
                               # (>= BB's ~2.5 s lead floor — a shorter lead comes back
                               #  REJECTED_BB / CANT_MAKE_LEAD)
---
bool success                   # True iff the ball was CAUGHT
string outcome                 # CAUGHT | REJECTED_<code> | ABORTED_<code> | MISSED | MISSED_<code>
float64 catch_error_mm         # mocap miss distance at rest (NaN if unknown)
---
string phase                   # CHECKING | AIMING | THROW_PENDING | BALL_IN_FLIGHT | CATCHING | SETTLING
